# host/deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore — P22A2, the deny-first build-context fence for
# host/deploy/Dockerfile alone.
#
# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to a root .dockerignore, so this fence is
# scoped to this one image: no other build in this repository is affected, and no shared root file
# has to satisfy two builds with different needs at once.
#
# The first rule denies the ENTIRE context. Everything the image legitimately needs is then
# re-included one explicit path at a time. A deny list would do the opposite — it would admit every
# file added to this repository from tomorrow on unless somebody remembers to deny it, which is
# exactly how a fixture, a planning document, a .git directory or a credential reaches an image
# layer by default. Deny-first fails the other way: a path nobody named simply never arrives, and
# the build says so.
#
# What is re-included is stated at path granularity, not file granularity. Each `!` line below names
# one explicit runtime path, and a named DIRECTORY admits everything inside it — `!src` admits the
# whole src/ tree, including any file added under it tomorrow, and the same holds for host/python_asgi
# and host/js_asgi. The named set is the npm lock pair for `npm ci`, the real src/ boundary the P22A1
# wrapper ultimately reaches through host/js_asgi, the Python host distribution's own build inputs,
# and the two host/deploy files the image installs from.
#
# Everything that is not one of those paths, or inside one of them, stays excluded by the leading `*`:
# tests, planning, db, docs, consumers, .git, .github and node_modules are deliberately absent from
# the list below and therefore never enter the context. So growth INSIDE a named directory needs no
# edit here and reaches a layer automatically; only a genuinely new top-level runtime path has to be
# added by hand, and until it is, the build fails loudly rather than shipping it silently.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src
!host/pyproject.toml
!host/python_asgi
!host/js_asgi
!host/deploy/secret_file_runner.mjs
!host/deploy/requirements-uvicorn.txt
